 York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dev C. Ittycheria | Interim President & CEO and Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $656,743 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $426K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 41%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $86K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $95K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["MongoDB, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $25.2B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +24% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +7.2pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -37% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $500M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -15.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -43.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.6%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 22% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 498% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.975277049255832},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $25.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why MongoDB (MDB) Could Beat Earnings Estimates Again","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025812/why-mongodb-mdb-could-beat-earnings-estimates-again?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_7-3025812","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793981401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MongoDB (NASDAQ:MDB) Stock: Insider C